<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Hilal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Hilal were an Arab tribal confederation from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> who migrated through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in the 11th century, encouraged by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> to punish the Zirids for breaking with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. From the 1050s they defeated the Zirids, ravaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> and pushed the Hammadids to the coast. Their arrival spread Arabic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pastoralism">pastoralism</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> and inspired the epic Taghribat Bani Hilal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banu-hilal.jpg" alt="Banu Hilal" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SPQR10 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pre_Islamic_Arabian_Tribes_(Harold_Dixon).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
